  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ab16c4c9be9f4134e9e1280441fa2bbc, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MunicipalRecord
  interactionName: Old Equipment Log
  isInformationSource: 1
  npcProfile: 0
  openingLine: It's been a quiet day around here.
  choice1: Ask about Daniel
  response1: Daniel Mercer disappeared seven years ago.
  choice2: Ask about the town
  response2: Nothing much changes around here.
  informationID: caleb_equipment_log
  informationTitle: Anonymous package
  informationSource: Anonymous package
  informationDescription: An anonymous sender sent me two waterworks records and a note claiming the original search missed something.
  informationType: 2
  isSceneExit: 0
  destinationScene: Diner_Investigation
  destinationSpawnID: 
  requiredInformationID: 
  unavailableMessage: These notes seem to refer to an old assignment. I should ask Caleb about his work at the waterworks before drawing conclusions from them.
  department: GRAYFORD MUNICIPAL RECORDS
  documentTitle: Equipment Service Log
  reference: Personal maintenance notebook
  documentDate: October 1991
  documentBody: "EQUIPMENT SERVICE LOG\r\nC. TURNER \u2014 PERSONAL NOTES\r\n\r\nOCTOBER 1991\r\n\r\nOCT 8\r\nPortable pump inspected. Intake hose replaced. Unit running normally.\r\n\r\nOCT 9\r\nPump and two work lamps issued for North County Waterworks assignment.\r\n\r\nOCT 10\r\nOne lamp returned with cracked housing. Replacement requested.\r\n\r\nPump return not entered.\r\n\r\nOCT 12\r\nFollowed up on missing equipment return. No confirmation received.\r\n\r\nADDITIONAL NOTES\r\n\r\nEntries are handwritten. Several later pages contain unrelated repair work.\r\n\r\nNo signed return receipt or completed field report is attached."
  evidenceID: caleb_equipment_log
  evidenceTitle: Caleb's Equipment Log
  journalNote: Caleb recorded a pump and two lamps for the October 9, 1991 waterworks job. One lamp returned damaged; no pump return is recorded.
  evidenceSource: Caleb Turner's Workshop
